100
06:34.880 --> 06:35.880
Seventh Company!

101
06:36.360 --> 06:37.390
Report!

102
06:37.680 --> 06:40.640
Seventh Company, one person present!

103
12:02.730 --> 12:05.380
On August 27, 1935,

104
12:05.900 --> 12:07.160
after six or seven days and nights of arduous trekking,

105
12:07.160 --> 12:09.920
the Right Route Army of the Red Army

106
12:10.060 --> 12:12.860
finally crossed the great grassland,

107
12:13.440 --> 12:15.600
known as a human death zone,

108
12:15.600 --> 12:18.000
at the cost of extremely heavy casualties.

109
12:18.000 --> 12:19.600
The Songpan Great Grassland

110
12:20.040 --> 12:21.640
is located in the transition zone

111
12:21.640 --> 12:24.510
between the Qinghai-Tibet Plateau and the Sichuan Basin.

112
12:24.510 --> 12:26.120
It was formed

113
12:26.120 --> 12:27.910
12,600 years ago.

114
12:28.750 --> 12:31.630
That was the Upper Paleolithic Period of mankind.

115
12:32.390 --> 12:35.080
It is also the source of an important tributary of the Yellow River,

116
12:35.080 --> 12:37.480
the mother river of the Chinese nation.

117
12:38.790 --> 12:40.150
Today,

118
12:40.670 --> 12:43.120
standing in the 21st century

119
12:43.200 --> 12:45.360
and looking back at that period of history,

120
12:45.360 --> 12:46.840
it is hard for us to truly understand

121
12:46.840 --> 12:49.360
how difficult and harsh

122
12:49.870 --> 12:52.240
that march 90 years ago was.

123
12:53.320 --> 12:54.670
But we should never

124
12:54.670 --> 12:56.400
forget that period of history.

125
12:56.910 --> 12:59.490
We should always remember those pioneers.

126
13:00.120 --> 13:01.120
It was they who,

127
13:01.870 --> 13:04.080
in this area defined by modern civilization

128
13:04.080 --> 13:05.870
as a "forbidden zone for life,"

129
13:05.960 --> 13:08.870
with unlined garments as armor and faith as shields,

130
13:08.870 --> 13:11.270
and with their feet in straw sandals,

131
13:11.440 --> 13:13.750
redefined the resilience of life.

132
13:14.840 --> 13:16.910
In this great feat,

133
13:17.280 --> 13:18.550
the harsh environment

134
13:18.570 --> 13:21.300
became a furnace that forged the national spirit

135
13:21.600 --> 13:25.530
and tempered the most brilliant crystallization of the human spirit.

136
13:25.900 --> 13:30.110
[Songpan County, Sichuan; Banyou (Present-day Banyou Village, Zoige County)]

137
13:26.030 --> 13:28.640
Every pioneer who laid down their lives here

138
13:29.910 --> 13:31.310
will never be forgotten.

139
13:37.780 --> 13:40.020
We made it out of the grassland.

140
13:41.220 --> 13:44.460
We finally made it out of the grassland!

141
13:45.080 --> 13:47.150
We made it out of the grassland.

142
13:47.290 --> 13:47.890
We…

143
13:47.910 --> 13:49.640
We made it out of the grassland!

144
13:50.930 --> 13:52.640
We are out!

145
13:58.960 --> 14:00.360
We are out!

146
14:02.030 --> 14:03.000
We made it out!

147
14:04.330 --> 14:05.680
A cow dung hut.

148
14:06.790 --> 14:08.360
We are out!

149
14:09.300 --> 14:10.340
A cow dung hut.

150
14:13.870 --> 14:17.030
Finally. We finally made it out!

151
14:17.600 --> 14:18.670
We finally made it out!

152
14:18.670 --> 14:20.020
Make camp in place!

153
14:20.090 --> 14:21.480
Pitch the tents!

154
14:21.500 --> 14:23.420
Set up camp!

155
14:23.450 --> 14:25.290
Make camp in place!

156
14:25.540 --> 14:27.210
Pitch the tents!

157
14:27.240 --> 14:28.880
Make camp in place!

158
14:29.440 --> 14:30.790
Pitch the tents!

159
14:42.180 --> 14:43.130
Chairman.

160
14:43.960 --> 14:45.020
Is this cow dung hut

161
14:45.150 --> 14:46.480
really made of cow dung?

162
14:46.510 --> 14:48.040
Does it smell like cow dung?

163
14:48.440 --> 14:50.670
Go closer, smell it,

164
14:51.030 --> 14:52.030
and lick it.

165
15:01.120 --> 15:01.750
Chairman.

166
15:02.120 --> 15:03.490
Chairman Mao. Chairman Mao.

167
15:03.490 --> 15:05.160
Chairman Mao. Chairman Mao.

168
15:06.620 --> 15:07.280
Xiangqian.

169
15:07.340 --> 15:07.860
Bo Gu.

170
15:13.000 --> 15:14.500
-Comrade Xiangqian. -Comrade Bo Gu.

171
15:14.500 --> 15:16.010
Chairman, we made it out.

172
15:22.150 --> 15:23.000
Chairman.

173
15:23.600 --> 15:24.270
Luofu.

174
15:24.850 --> 15:25.570
Changhao.

175
15:25.620 --> 15:26.410
Luofu.

176
15:28.270 --> 15:29.120
Chairman.

177
15:29.860 --> 15:31.390
The cow dung doesn't stink.

178
15:33.360 --> 15:34.550
This cow dung hut

179
15:35.240 --> 15:36.720
is warm in winter and cool in summer.

180
15:36.720 --> 15:38.750
It guarantees everyone a good sleep.

181
15:38.750 --> 15:39.820
We

182
15:39.930 --> 15:41.600
have lived in buildings in Moscow,

183
15:41.600 --> 15:42.790
alleys in Shanghai,

184
15:43.080 --> 15:45.080
and tile-roofed houses in Jiangxi.

185
15:45.080 --> 15:46.200
On this Long March,

186
15:46.550 --> 15:48.910
we've also lived in civilian houses,

187
15:49.080 --> 15:52.030
temples, academies, watchtowers,

188
15:52.320 --> 15:53.600
Tusi Manors,

189
15:53.750 --> 15:54.480
tents,

190
15:54.630 --> 15:55.550
and caves.

191
15:55.840 --> 15:58.570
We've even sat on the grass and watched the stars.

192
15:58.750 --> 15:59.390
Today,

193
15:59.440 --> 16:03.400
for the first time ever, we're going to live in this cow dung hut.

194
16:05.390 --> 16:07.140
Gentlemen from the foreign houses,

195
16:07.140 --> 16:09.220
this is truly

196
16:09.550 --> 16:12.030
stepping into the land of China.

197
16:12.050 --> 16:13.050
Gentlemen,

198
16:13.400 --> 16:15.120
we've prepared a feast for you.

199
16:15.120 --> 16:15.390
Yes.

200
16:15.390 --> 16:16.530
Please come into the cow dung hut.

201
16:16.530 --> 16:17.390
Yes. Hurry. Come.

202
16:17.390 --> 16:18.630
Come, Chairman, let's go.

203
16:18.630 --> 16:19.820
Be careful, Chairman.

204
16:19.820 --> 16:20.580
Bo Gu.

205
16:22.630 --> 16:23.030
I'll do it.

206
16:23.030 --> 16:23.570
I'll help you.

207
16:23.570 --> 16:24.290
I'll do it.

208
16:24.390 --> 16:25.390
Hurry, go inside.

209
16:25.480 --> 16:26.080
Okay.

210
16:28.210 --> 16:30.110
The ancient grassland is a devil's field,

211
16:30.110 --> 16:31.910
with no birds or beasts in sight.

212
16:31.950 --> 16:33.840
Every Red Army soldier is a man of steel.

213
16:33.840 --> 16:36.730
They charge through dragon's lairs and tiger's dens.

214
16:36.730 --> 16:38.460
The grassland sees four seasons in a day,

215
16:38.460 --> 16:41.190
with wind, rain, thunder, lightning, and frost.

216
16:44.810 --> 16:45.680
Little Big Brother.

217
16:45.680 --> 16:46.610
4th Big Brother.

218
16:46.690 --> 16:47.880
We've joined forces again.

219
16:47.880 --> 16:49.540
Don't call me 4th Big Brother.

220
16:49.710 --> 16:51.020
Let's formally introduce ourselves.

221
16:50.610 --> 16:52.990
[Zhang Side, Soldier of the 4th Front Army]

222
16:52.330 --> 16:53.280
My name is Zhang Side.

223
16:53.090 --> 16:54.230
[Xie Xingguo, Publicist of the Publicity team of the 1st Red Army Corps]

224
16:53.300 --> 16:54.560
My name is Xie Xingguo.

225
16:58.780 --> 17:00.370
Here, take this.

226
17:03.060 --> 17:04.010
You eat it.

227
17:04.849 --> 17:05.720
Take it.

228
17:08.220 --> 17:09.109
Comrade Side,

229
17:09.829 --> 17:11.680
you always bring me food,

230
17:11.910 --> 17:13.569
but I have nothing to give you.

231
17:13.640 --> 17:16.890
Comrade Xingguo, this is a gift.

232
17:17.829 --> 17:19.490
It's spiritual nourishment.

233
17:19.640 --> 17:20.530
Goodbye.

234
17:21.720 --> 17:22.680
Goodbye.

235
17:24.109 --> 17:25.589
Comrades, press on with all your might.

236
17:25.589 --> 17:27.550
Walk out of the grassland and we'll see the clear sky.

237
17:27.550 --> 17:29.240
Comrades, keep your fighting spirit high.

238
17:29.240 --> 17:30.720
We fear neither death nor injury.

239
17:30.720 --> 17:31.790
The revolutionary spirit is our faith.

240
17:31.790 --> 17:33.400
You help me, I help you.

241
17:33.400 --> 17:35.050
Comrades-in-arms are closer than brothers.

242
17:35.050 --> 17:36.800
Cherish our class bond together.

243
17:36.800 --> 17:39.000
With one heart, we cross the grassland.

244
17:45.500 --> 17:47.370
The ancient grassland is a devil's field,

245
17:47.370 --> 17:49.170
with no birds or beasts in sight.

246
17:49.240 --> 17:50.980
Every Red Army soldier is a man of steel.

247
17:50.980 --> 17:52.830
They charge through dragon's lairs and tiger's dens.

248
17:52.830 --> 17:54.550
The grassland sees four seasons in a day,

249
17:54.550 --> 17:57.280
with wind, rain, thunder, lightning, and frost.

250
18:17.820 --> 18:18.690
Drink slowly.

251
18:20.530 --> 18:22.290
Here, have a piece of meat.

252
18:23.430 --> 18:24.360
Here, Chairman.

253
18:32.470 --> 18:34.200
Here, Jianying, Comrade Bo Gu.

254
18:34.310 --> 18:35.440
Have a piece of meat.

255
18:35.680 --> 18:36.440
Chairman.

256
18:36.930 --> 18:37.760
Have a piece.

257
18:39.370 --> 18:40.400
Look at this young comrade.

258
18:40.400 --> 18:40.720
Bo Gu.

259
18:40.720 --> 18:41.790
There's so much but it's not enough for you to eat?

260
18:41.790 --> 18:44.050
You're even putting some in your pocket.

261
18:44.130 --> 18:46.790
I'm afraid the Chairman will be hungry at night.

262
18:48.270 --> 18:49.480
You are blatantly

263
18:49.510 --> 18:51.040
using Chairman Mao's name.

264
18:54.350 --> 18:55.550
There's plenty, there's plenty.

265
18:55.550 --> 18:56.480
Take it, take it.

266
18:56.500 --> 18:57.360
That's enough.

267
18:58.050 --> 18:59.380
Put them in your pocket.

268
18:59.400 --> 19:00.330
Take more.

269
19:00.790 --> 19:01.350
Come.

270
19:01.960 --> 19:02.700
Alright, here.

271
19:02.700 --> 19:04.760
Jianying, brief us on the situation.

272
19:05.000 --> 19:05.480
Okay.

273
19:05.720 --> 19:06.440
Xiangqian.

274
19:07.230 --> 19:07.750
Come.

275
19:11.270 --> 19:13.750
After our Right-Flank Advance Force reached Banyou,

276
19:13.750 --> 19:14.940
we immediately investigated

277
19:14.940 --> 19:16.490
the route to southern Gansu.

278
19:16.490 --> 19:18.220
If we follow the original plan,

279
19:18.440 --> 19:20.100
it will take four days

280
19:20.190 --> 19:21.520
from Banyou to Labrang.

281
19:21.780 --> 19:23.630
And we have to pass through the grassland again.

282
19:23.540 --> 19:26.150
[Ye Jianying, Chief of Staff of the Red Army Frontline General Headquarters]

283
19:23.690 --> 19:25.200
We may encounter harassment

284
19:25.200 --> 19:27.130
from the KMT cavalry along the way.

285
19:29.350 --> 19:30.520
Is there a better route?

286
19:30.520 --> 19:31.250
There is one.

287
19:38.440 --> 19:39.570
Chairman Mao, look.

288
19:39.630 --> 19:42.390
If we turn northeast from Banyou,

289
19:42.550 --> 19:44.640
pass through Baxi to Baozuo,

290
19:44.640 --> 19:45.640
and then to E'jie,

291
19:45.790 --> 19:47.090
we can follow the Songpan-Gansu Ancient Road

292
19:47.090 --> 19:48.690
directly to southern Gansu.

293
19:48.730 --> 19:49.450
With this route,

294
19:49.450 --> 19:50.580
we don't have to cross the grassland again.

295
19:50.410 --> 19:52.830
[Xu Xiangqian, Commander-in-Chief of the Red Army Frontline General Headquarters and of the 4th Front Army]

296
19:50.600 --> 19:51.550
The distance is also shorter.

297
19:51.550 --> 19:53.110
There are many villages along the way,

298
19:53.110 --> 19:54.530
so supplies won't be a problem.

299
19:54.530 --> 19:56.930
It's suitable for our large forces to move.

300
19:57.420 --> 19:59.870
But the only difficulty with this route is

301
20:00.080 --> 20:01.330
that we have to pass through Baozuo.

302
20:01.330 --> 20:03.930
An elite unit of Hu Zongnan is stationed there.

303
20:04.340 --> 20:06.000
We might have to fight a battle.

304
20:06.000 --> 20:06.850
Back then,

305
20:06.880 --> 20:08.220
if our "Songpan Campaign Plan"

306
20:08.220 --> 20:09.450
had been successfully carried out,

307
20:09.450 --> 20:11.200
Hu Zongnan would have had no chance

308
20:11.200 --> 20:12.270
to station troops in Baozuo.

309
20:12.270 --> 20:14.960
And we would have already moved along the Songpan-Gansu Ancient Road

310
20:14.960 --> 20:17.020
and reached southern Gansu long ago.

311
20:19.830 --> 20:21.390
The 25th Division of the Left Route Army

312
20:21.390 --> 20:22.870
has already occupied Aba,

313
20:22.550 --> 20:25.750
[Chen Changhao, Director of the General Political Department of Red Army; Political Commissar of the Red Army Frontline General Headquarters and the 4th Front Army]

314
20:23.120 --> 20:24.580
but most of the main forces

315
20:24.700 --> 20:26.590
are still stuck along the Zhuokeji line.

316
20:26.590 --> 20:29.920
Regarding the telegram that Xiangqian and I sent jointly earlier,

317
20:29.920 --> 20:31.470
Comrade Guotao still

318
20:31.570 --> 20:32.850
hasn't given a clear reply.

319
20:32.850 --> 20:35.640
Comrade Guotao still lacks confidence

320
20:35.920 --> 20:36.880
and is hesitant.

321
20:37.160 --> 20:37.970
Old habit.

322
20:38.940 --> 20:40.570
Zhang Guotao's old habit.

323
20:42.590 --> 20:43.440
So,

324
20:44.480 --> 20:46.510
we have to urge him not only by telegram

325
20:46.510 --> 20:48.370
but also with practical actions.

326
20:49.090 --> 20:50.160
Take down Baozuo,

327
20:50.510 --> 20:52.240
control the Songpan-Gansu Ancient Road,

328
20:52.240 --> 20:54.970
and win time for the Left Route Army to move north.

329
20:57.160 --> 20:58.990
On August 26, 1935,

330
20:59.650 --> 21:03.240
the Right Route Army canceled its original marching plan in Banyou

331
21:03.240 --> 21:04.970
and headed northeast.

332
21:05.800 --> 21:07.280
By August 27,

333
21:07.590 --> 21:09.930
they successively occupied Baxi, Shangzang Temple,

334
21:09.930 --> 21:12.860
Yanong Village, Jiaji, Panzhou, and other places,

335
21:13.270 --> 21:13.720
cutting off

336
21:13.720 --> 21:16.650
the communication between Qiuji Temple and Axirong

337
21:16.860 --> 21:20.430
and laying the foundation for launching the Baozuo Campaign.

338
21:22.640 --> 21:25.970
[Songpan, Sichuan; Hu Zongnan's Headquarters]

339
21:23.550 --> 21:24.640
Is the intelligence accurate?

340
21:24.640 --> 21:25.510
Absolutely accurate.

341
21:25.510 --> 21:27.680
The main Communist forces have already crossed the grassland,

342
21:27.680 --> 21:28.600
heading northeast from Banyou

343
21:28.600 --> 21:29.840
towards Baozuo.

344
21:30.030 --> 21:32.400
The air force in Chongqing also confirmed this intelligence.

345
21:32.400 --> 21:34.530
The Generalissimo probably knows about it too by now.

346
21:33.280 --> 21:37.220
[Hu Zongnan, Commander of the 2nd Column of the 3rd Route Army of the KMT's Communist Suppression Forces]

347
21:36.000 --> 21:38.600
What on earth are these people's bones made of?

348
21:43.170 --> 21:43.750
Yes.

349
21:44.710 --> 21:45.310
Yes.

350
21:45.860 --> 21:47.060
Commander Hu is here.

351
21:48.190 --> 21:50.590
It's the Generalissimo calling from Emei.

352
22:00.960 --> 22:02.070
Greetings, Principal.

353
22:02.070 --> 22:03.150
This is Hu Zongnan.

354
22:02.970 --> 22:06.680
[Mount Emei, Sichuan]

355
22:03.480 --> 22:05.160
What are your thoughts on the Communist Army

356
22:05.160 --> 22:07.020
crossing the Songpan Grassland?

357
22:07.440 --> 22:10.500
I think the Communist Army is at the end of its strength.

358
22:10.720 --> 22:11.000
They…

359
22:11.000 --> 22:12.720
Stop deceiving yourself.

360
22:13.160 --> 22:14.620
At the end of its strength?

361
22:14.830 --> 22:16.370
Draw a division from your troops

362
22:16.370 --> 22:17.960
and see how they march across it.

363
22:17.960 --> 22:20.370
I think the Communist Army is gaining momentum

364
22:20.370 --> 22:22.720
and has already circled around behind you.

365
22:22.720 --> 22:23.190
Yes.

366
22:23.740 --> 22:26.180
It was my oversight. Please punish me, Principal.

367
22:26.180 --> 22:27.620
Shoushan,

368
22:28.400 --> 22:30.980
no need to be hypocritical with me.

369
22:31.600 --> 22:34.080
If the Communist Army was merely feinting

370
22:34.100 --> 22:35.750
in Yunnan and Guizhou before,

371
22:35.750 --> 22:36.590
then now it is

372
22:36.590 --> 22:38.440
blatantly heading north.

373
22:39.050 --> 22:41.400
If they successfully pass through southern Gansu

374
22:41.400 --> 22:42.440
and join forces with Xu Haidong

375
22:42.440 --> 22:44.640
or the Communist Army in northern Shaanxi,

376
22:44.640 --> 22:46.920
it will be a disaster for the Party.

377
22:47.370 --> 22:48.440
I understand.

378
22:48.640 --> 22:50.030
Please rest assured, Principal.

379
22:50.030 --> 22:52.300
The Communist Army must go through Baozuo to march north.

380
22:52.300 --> 22:54.850
I will send troops to reinforce Baozuo immediately.

381
22:54.850 --> 22:56.090
We will stop the Communist Army

382
22:56.090 --> 22:58.440
at the Baozuo River line at all costs.

383
22:58.670 --> 22:59.670
Don't let me down.

384
22:59.780 --> 23:00.320
Yes, sir.

385
23:13.370 --> 23:15.170
First, the bandit situation.

386
23:15.370 --> 23:17.230
Second, the Japanese situation.

387
23:17.250 --> 23:20.680
Third, the principle of dealing with bandits before the Japanese.

388
23:20.680 --> 23:22.470
None should be forgotten.

389
23:27.170 --> 23:28.640
Send a telegram to Wu Chengren.

390
23:28.640 --> 23:31.110
Order the 49th Division to reinforce Baozuo immediately.

391
23:31.110 --> 23:31.960
Without fail.

392
23:32.160 --> 23:32.890
Yes, sir.

393
23:34.680 --> 23:41.230
[Axi, Songpan, Sichuan; Temporary Encampment of the Central Committee]

394
23:40.060 --> 23:41.540
Baozuo

395
23:41.750 --> 23:43.410
is divided by the Baozuo River

396
23:43.470 --> 23:45.470
into Upper Baozuo and Lower Baozuo.

397
23:46.290 --> 23:47.990
According to the intelligence we have now,

398
23:47.990 --> 23:50.320
Hu Zongnan's troops have one battalion stationed at the Dajie Temple

399
23:50.320 --> 23:51.320
in Upper Baozuo

400
23:51.650 --> 23:53.050
and one regiment at the Qiuji Temple

401
23:53.050 --> 23:53.980
in Lower Baozuo.

402
23:54.120 --> 23:54.880
In addition,

403
23:55.150 --> 23:57.590
Hu Zongnan's main force, the 49th Division under Wu Chengren,

404
23:57.590 --> 23:59.380
is also moving to reinforce Baozuo.

405
23:59.380 --> 24:00.900
The troop strength is about 12,000 people.

406
24:00.900 --> 24:02.880
This battle must be fought quickly.

407
24:02.880 --> 24:03.880
We not only have to take Baozuo

408
24:03.880 --> 24:05.470
but also deal with Wu Chengren's reinforcements

409
24:05.470 --> 24:06.810
and control the Songpan-Gansu Ancient Road.

410
24:06.810 --> 24:08.140
I agree with Xiangqian.

411
24:08.200 --> 24:09.340
If our attack doesn't go well,

412
24:09.340 --> 24:11.440
once Hu Zongnan's tens of thousands of troops arrive as reinforcements,

413
24:11.440 --> 24:13.880
we could very well be forced back to the Songpan Grassland.

414
24:13.880 --> 24:15.800
What is your specific operational deployment?

415
24:15.800 --> 24:16.670
Which unit

416
24:16.990 --> 24:18.930
will complete the task of attacking Baozuo?

417
24:18.930 --> 24:20.440
The 1st Red Army is severely fatigued.

418
24:20.440 --> 24:21.960
The 3rd Red Army has not walked out of the grassland yet.

419
24:21.960 --> 24:23.110
So this time,

420
24:23.550 --> 24:24.960
our Fourth Red Army will attack Baozuo.

421
24:24.960 --> 24:26.270
I want to arrange it like this.

422
24:26.270 --> 24:28.270
The 264th Regiment of the 89th Division of the 30th Red Army

423
24:28.270 --> 24:30.260
will be responsible for attacking Dajie Temple in Upper Baozuo.

424
24:30.260 --> 24:31.500
The 10th Division of the Fourth Red Army

425
24:31.500 --> 24:33.400
will be responsible for attacking Qiuji Temple in Lower Baozuo.

426
24:33.400 --> 24:34.640
In addition, the 88th Division

427
24:34.640 --> 24:36.510
and the other two regiments of the 89th Division

428
24:36.510 --> 24:38.270
will quickly set up an ambush in the mountain forest northwest of Upper Baozuo,

429
24:38.270 --> 24:40.030
ready to intercept the reinforcements at any time.

430
24:40.030 --> 24:42.590
The 30th Red Army and the Fourth Red Army of the 4th Front Army

431
24:42.590 --> 24:44.240
have also just walked out of the grassland

432
24:44.240 --> 24:45.700
and are equally fatigued.

433
24:46.490 --> 24:47.300
At least

434
24:47.540 --> 24:50.140
we're a bit better than your 1st Front Red Army.

435
24:50.510 --> 24:51.640
Better in what way?

436
24:53.430 --> 24:55.120
At least we

437
24:55.310 --> 24:56.640
walked out of the grassland two days earlier than you.

438
24:56.640 --> 24:58.620
We also ate tree bark and wild vegetables for two more days

439
24:58.620 --> 25:00.220
and rested for two more days.

440
25:00.260 --> 25:00.870
Also,

441
25:01.020 --> 25:02.190
no matter you or us,

442
25:02.210 --> 25:03.400
the 1st Red Army or the 4th Red Army,

443
25:03.400 --> 25:04.220
we are all the Red Army.

444
25:04.220 --> 25:05.620
Being the Red Army means we are one family.

445
25:05.620 --> 25:07.350
Why talk like we are strangers?

446
25:11.550 --> 25:12.390
Xiangqian,

447
25:13.400 --> 25:14.750
well said!

448
25:15.350 --> 25:16.960
Family doesn't talk like strangers.

449
25:16.960 --> 25:17.790
Unity.

450
25:18.200 --> 25:20.530
This is what our Red Army should look like.

451
25:22.440 --> 25:23.270
I think

452
25:23.830 --> 25:26.550
we can telegraph the operational plan for the Baozuo Campaign

453
25:26.550 --> 25:27.750
to the Left Route Army

454
25:27.920 --> 25:29.780
and also let Comrade Zhang Guotao

455
25:29.790 --> 25:31.250
know our good intentions,

456
25:31.440 --> 25:33.030
hoping he can seriously consider

457
25:33.030 --> 25:34.000
marching north immediately.

458
25:34.000 --> 25:34.750
Okay.

459
25:34.920 --> 25:35.510
Okay.

460
25:41.200 --> 25:44.240
On the night of August 29, 1935,

461
25:44.850 --> 25:46.960
the Red Army simultaneously launched attacks

462
25:46.960 --> 25:49.420
on Dajie Temple and Qiuji Temple garrisoned by the enemy

463
25:49.420 --> 25:50.880
in Upper and Lower Baozuo.

464
25:52.000 --> 25:54.070
Relying on solid fortifications and superior equipment,

465
25:54.070 --> 25:56.470
the enemy fought desperately.

466
25:57.310 --> 25:59.880
The Red Army, lacking heavy weapons and sufficient ammunition,

467
25:59.880 --> 26:01.440
found it hard to take the position.

468
26:01.440 --> 26:03.850
The battle has reached a stalemate.

469
26:05.680 --> 26:06.970
During the fierce fighting,

470
26:06.970 --> 26:10.400
Wang Youjun, Commander of the 10th Division of the Fourth Red Army,

471
26:10.400 --> 26:11.940
heroically sacrificed his life.

472
26:11.940 --> 26:16.330
[Upper Baozuo, Sichuan; Headquarters of the 30th Red Army]

473
26:15.060 --> 26:15.780
Shicai.

474
26:16.690 --> 26:17.290
Xiannian.

475
26:17.550 --> 26:18.110
Commander-in-Chief.

476
26:18.110 --> 26:19.310
How is the situation?

477
26:20.070 --> 26:21.110
The 264th Regiment has already occupied

478
26:21.110 --> 26:22.440
the outer positions of Dajie Temple.

479
26:22.440 --> 26:24.160
But the enemy retreated into the temple and put up a desperate last-ditch resistance.

480
26:24.160 --> 26:26.560
We lack heavy weapons, so we can't break in.

481
26:26.930 --> 26:27.920
Commander-in-Chief.

482
26:27.920 --> 26:29.780
How is the battle at Qiuji Temple?

483
26:30.370 --> 26:32.300
The situation is similar to yours.

484
26:33.730 --> 26:35.530
Division Commander Wang Youjun

485
26:36.730 --> 26:38.590
heroically sacrificed his life.

486
26:39.260 --> 26:42.180
[Cheng Shicai, Commander of the 30th Red Army]

487
26:43.120 --> 26:44.690
I'll lead the commando team up there myself.

488
26:44.690 --> 26:46.490
Xu Shiyou told me the same thing.

489
26:48.620 --> 26:50.660
We've already lost a division commander.

490
26:50.660 --> 26:52.720
Are we going to lose an army commander

491
26:53.210 --> 26:54.890
and more soldiers?

492
26:56.760 --> 26:57.890
If relying solely on not fearing death

493
26:57.890 --> 26:59.350
was enough to win battles,

494
26:59.570 --> 27:01.030
we would have won long ago.

495
27:03.730 --> 27:04.990
Then what should we do?

496
27:06.180 --> 27:07.310
Change our tactics.

497
27:08.160 --> 27:09.330
From now on,

498
27:09.560 --> 27:11.510
change all assaults to sieges.

499
27:11.530 --> 27:13.860
While reducing unnecessary casualties,

500
27:13.880 --> 27:14.920
continue to put pressure on the enemy,

501
27:14.920 --> 27:18.160
but don't apply maximum pressure.

502
27:18.180 --> 27:19.140
Understand?

503
27:21.910 --> 27:22.910
Lure the enemy.

504
27:24.030 --> 27:24.500
Attack the reinforcements.

505
27:24.500 --> 27:25.150
Right.

506
27:25.790 --> 27:26.830
Our main target

507
27:26.880 --> 27:28.630
is Wu Chengren's 49th Division.

508
27:28.630 --> 27:29.720
He is currently

509
27:29.830 --> 27:31.160
about one day's journey from Baozuo.

510
27:31.160 --> 27:32.490
We will set up an ambush,

511
27:32.710 --> 27:33.840
fight while we wait.

512
27:33.840 --> 27:34.570
Understood.

513
27:35.640 --> 27:37.970
I heard that Wu Chengren, like Hu Zongnan,

514
27:38.070 --> 27:40.200
was your classmate in the first class of Whampoa.

515
27:40.200 --> 27:40.920
Yes.

516
27:41.750 --> 27:44.280
We were in the same class but different teams.

517
27:44.310 --> 27:46.270
He was in the third team,

518
27:46.680 --> 27:47.810
the same team as Chen Geng.

519
27:47.810 --> 27:49.450
Then we must catch him this time,

520
27:49.450 --> 27:51.980
so you old classmates can have a good reunion.

521
27:54.350 --> 27:55.550
I have no objections.

522
28:00.520 --> 28:01.450
Here's the plan.

523
28:01.850 --> 28:03.050
Shicai, Xiannian.

524
28:03.200 --> 28:03.800
Remember.

525
28:03.970 --> 28:06.410
As soon as the advance unit of the 49th Division arrives,

526
28:06.410 --> 28:07.670
our troops will retreat immediately.

527
28:07.670 --> 28:10.860
But we must not rush.

528
28:11.140 --> 28:13.000
We need to let all of Wu Chengren's main forces

529
28:13.000 --> 28:14.330
come in completely.

530
28:14.510 --> 28:16.240
Once their main forces arrive,

531
28:16.270 --> 28:18.510
we will surround them here.

532
28:18.620 --> 28:20.100
Teach my old classmate

533
28:20.990 --> 28:21.950
a lesson.

534
28:23.310 --> 28:23.990
Yes, sir.

535
28:27.390 --> 28:29.720
On August 31, 1935,

536
28:30.590 --> 28:33.440
the main forces of the 49th Division of the Kuomintang Central Army

537
28:33.440 --> 28:36.310
all entered the ambush area of the 30th Red Army.

538
28:38.750 --> 28:39.830
At 5:00 p.m.,

539
28:39.850 --> 28:41.080
the battle began.

540
28:41.840 --> 28:44.800
The 268th Regiment of the Red Army took the lead in rushing down the hillside,

541
28:44.800 --> 28:46.260
heading straight at the Baozuo Bridge,

542
28:46.260 --> 28:49.740
the core of the front line of the KMT troops' 49th Division.

543
28:50.930 --> 28:52.200
Like an iron plow,

544
28:52.310 --> 28:55.400
it plowed a bloody path through the Kuomintang troops,

545
28:53.500 --> 28:55.540
[Wu Chengren, Commander of the 49th Division of the KMT troops]

546
28:55.790 --> 28:58.090
cutting the three regiments of the KMT's 49th Division

547
28:58.090 --> 28:59.440
into three sections.

548
28:59.920 --> 29:01.660
Seeing that the situation was bad,

549
29:01.660 --> 29:03.850
Wu Chengren personally organized his troops to counterattack.

550
29:03.850 --> 29:05.320
They attacked the 268th Regiment

551
29:05.320 --> 29:07.560
on both banks of the Baozuo River.

552
29:08.170 --> 29:10.570
The 268th Regiment of the Red Army dashed left and right

553
29:10.570 --> 29:13.500
and broke the enemy's charges several times in a row.

554
29:13.550 --> 29:15.410
It held the Baozuo Bridge firmly,

555
29:15.710 --> 29:18.110
while suffering heavy casualties itself.

556
29:20.360 --> 29:21.680
At the critical moment,

557
29:21.680 --> 29:23.000
Cheng Shicai and Li Xiannian

558
29:23.000 --> 29:25.830
ordered the troops to launch a full-scale attack.

559
29:26.430 --> 29:27.490
Under conditions of

560
29:27.490 --> 29:29.540
extreme fatigue, hunger,

561
29:29.570 --> 29:32.170
and an extreme lack of weapons and ammunition,

562
29:32.460 --> 29:34.030
all commanders and fighters of the 30th Red Army,

563
29:34.030 --> 29:35.440
from Commander Cheng Shicai and Political Commissar Li Xiannian

564
29:35.440 --> 29:37.590
to guards, messengers,

565
29:37.670 --> 29:39.360
publicists, cooks,

566
29:39.380 --> 29:41.620
and animal handlers,

567
29:41.720 --> 29:43.580
threw themselves into the battle

568
29:43.870 --> 29:46.030
and fought the enemy.

569
29:47.170 --> 29:49.720
The fighting lasted until the early morning of September 1,

570
29:49.720 --> 29:52.720
and the KMT's 49th Division was completely defeated.

571
29:52.920 --> 29:54.720
Except for the seriously wounded Division Commander Wu Chengren,

572
29:54.720 --> 29:55.980
who narrowly escaped,

573
29:56.300 --> 29:58.230
most of the rest were annihilated.

574
29:59.240 --> 30:00.330
Many years later,

575
30:00.570 --> 30:01.680
General Cheng Shicai

576
30:01.680 --> 30:03.920
recalled this battle and said,

577
30:04.680 --> 30:07.090
"When we passed this position,

578
30:07.430 --> 30:08.830
almost every step we took

579
30:08.940 --> 30:11.140
would land on the blood of the martyrs."

580
30:13.790 --> 30:14.920
The Baozuo Campaign

581
30:14.960 --> 30:17.680
was the first major victory achieved

582
30:17.700 --> 30:20.160
after the 1st and 4th Front Red Armies joined forces.

583
30:20.160 --> 30:21.880
It shattered the KMT troops' attempt

584
30:21.880 --> 30:25.410
to trap the Red Army in the grasslands of northwestern Sichuan.

585
30:26.070 --> 30:26.870
With this,

586
30:27.290 --> 30:30.820
the Right Route Army of the Red Army completely walked out of the grassland,

587
30:30.820 --> 30:32.690
cleared the passage to the north,

588
30:32.810 --> 30:36.210
and opened the gateway to advance north into southern Gansu.

589
30:37.430 --> 30:42.280
[Mount Emei, Sichuan]

590
30:38.110 --> 30:39.040
Generalissimo.

591
30:39.200 --> 30:40.020
This is the list of graduates

592
30:40.020 --> 30:41.770
from the first class of the Emei Officers Training Corps.

593
30:41.770 --> 30:42.600
I've made marks

594
30:42.600 --> 30:45.000
under the names of the outstanding cadets.

595
30:45.080 --> 30:45.730
Good.

596
30:45.980 --> 30:47.420
These people on the list

597
30:47.720 --> 30:49.180
must be repeatedly tested

598
30:49.180 --> 30:50.420
and carefully screened.

599
30:50.420 --> 30:50.950
Yes, sir.

600
30:51.070 --> 30:52.030
Don't be like me

601
30:52.160 --> 30:53.830
back at Whampoa,

602
30:53.850 --> 30:56.610
misjudging people like Chen Geng.

603
30:57.370 --> 30:58.700
I remember at that time,

604
30:58.980 --> 31:00.150
Xu Xiangqian,

605
31:00.330 --> 31:01.160
thin and tall,

606
31:01.510 --> 31:03.300
spoke with a thick Shanxi accent

607
31:03.300 --> 31:06.020
and was reserved when talking to me.

608
31:06.590 --> 31:07.630
But look,

609
31:07.650 --> 31:09.510
in Sujiabu of Hubei-Henan-Anhui

610
31:09.710 --> 31:11.260
and the Daba Mountains of Sichuan,

611
31:11.260 --> 31:12.460
his command ability

612
31:12.600 --> 31:15.340
showed the talent of those from Whampoa.

613
31:15.400 --> 31:16.030
Indeed.

614
31:16.230 --> 31:17.830
And look at Wu Chengren.

615
31:18.110 --> 31:20.400
Back then, when he answered questions,

616
31:20.510 --> 31:22.920
he was so impassioned and resolute.

617
31:23.270 --> 31:24.800
But in the Baozuo Campaign,

618
31:25.130 --> 31:26.330
he neither succeeded

619
31:26.640 --> 31:27.900
nor died for the cause.

620
31:28.160 --> 31:28.960
I think

621
31:29.080 --> 31:30.740
we should just let Wu Chengren

622
31:30.800 --> 31:32.260
die for the cause himself.

623
31:33.420 --> 31:34.840
Please calm down, Generalissimo.

624
31:34.840 --> 31:35.720
These past few days,

625
31:35.720 --> 31:36.970
many Whampoa alumni,

626
31:37.000 --> 31:38.510
including Shoushan (Hu Zongnan),

627
31:38.510 --> 31:40.880
have been pleading for Division Commander Wu Chengren.

628
31:40.880 --> 31:42.570
They hope you'll show him some leniency.

629
31:42.570 --> 31:43.770
What's your opinion?

630
31:45.790 --> 31:46.660
In my humble opinion,

631
31:46.660 --> 31:49.050
there's a reason

632
31:49.160 --> 31:50.750
for Division Commander Wu's disastrous defeat.

633
31:50.750 --> 31:52.350
We are in need of people right now,

634
31:52.350 --> 31:54.640
so I hope you will think it over carefully, Generalissimo.

635
31:54.640 --> 31:57.070
I knew you all would plead for him.

636
31:57.960 --> 31:59.130
I can't let Wu Chengren

637
31:59.130 --> 32:00.810
command troops again.

638
32:01.030 --> 32:02.830
I think we should remove him from his post

639
32:02.830 --> 32:04.760
and send him to the Army War College

640
32:04.830 --> 32:06.420
to study for a few more years.

641
32:06.420 --> 32:08.510
Yes. You are merciful, Generalissimo.

642
32:08.510 --> 32:09.230
By the way,

643
32:09.400 --> 32:11.240
I ordered Shoushan to go from Songpan to Xigu,

644
32:11.240 --> 32:12.590
detouring through Wenxian,

645
32:12.590 --> 32:13.580
to intercept the Communist Army.

646
32:13.580 --> 32:14.630
Has he replied?

647
32:15.490 --> 32:17.360
Shoushan has just replied.

648
32:17.770 --> 32:18.820
He said

649
32:18.990 --> 32:20.790
it's too risky to go north alone.

650
32:20.820 --> 32:22.000
They should postpone setting out

651
32:22.000 --> 32:24.990
until Xue Yue's troops are deployed along the Songpan line.

652
32:24.990 --> 32:27.000
Once the flanks are secure, they'll set off.

653
32:27.000 --> 32:28.270
None of these guys

654
32:28.510 --> 32:30.000
are useful.

655
32:30.680 --> 32:32.830
Arrange for these people on the list.

656
32:32.850 --> 32:34.000
I want to meet them,

657
32:34.310 --> 32:36.310
give them a talk, and call the roll.

658
32:36.790 --> 32:38.160
Reporting to the Generalissimo,

659
32:38.160 --> 32:39.220
they have been gathered

660
32:39.220 --> 32:41.220
and are waiting for you downstairs.

661
32:41.550 --> 32:43.410
Cixiu is the one who knows me best.

662
32:49.250 --> 32:49.790
Let's go.

663
32:54.160 --> 33:00.570
[Yanong Village, Baxi, Sichuan]

664
32:54.690 --> 32:56.060
In the Baozuo Campaign,

665
32:56.360 --> 32:59.230
our army inflicted heavy losses on the enemy's 49th Division.

666
32:59.230 --> 33:00.950
We killed and wounded over 4,000 people,

667
33:00.950 --> 33:02.280
captured more than 800,

668
33:02.670 --> 33:05.400
and seized over 1,500 firearms of various types,

669
33:06.080 --> 33:08.410
as well as more than 50 light machine guns.

670
33:08.830 --> 33:10.890
This time we also captured a large amount of

671
33:10.890 --> 33:12.330
ammunition, food,

672
33:12.350 --> 33:13.210
and livestock.

673
33:13.510 --> 33:14.480
Yaks?

674
33:15.050 --> 33:15.850
Great!

675
33:16.400 --> 33:18.570
The comrades can improve their lives.

676
33:18.660 --> 33:19.390
In addition,

677
33:19.570 --> 33:21.100
after the Baozuo Campaign,

678
33:21.310 --> 33:23.390
Hu Zongnan didn't move north in time,

679
33:23.460 --> 33:25.480
which will lead to a large-scale military vacuum

680
33:25.480 --> 33:27.920
in the southern Gansu area.

681
33:28.200 --> 33:29.320
I've calculated it.

682
33:29.320 --> 33:30.450
From Baozuo to Xigu,

683
33:30.450 --> 33:31.830
and from Xigu to Minzhou,

684
33:31.830 --> 33:32.770
we can get there in six days.

685
33:32.770 --> 33:33.900
No, five days.

686
33:33.930 --> 33:35.390
I guarantee we'll arrive.

687
33:35.530 --> 33:38.130
That area is entirely a Han-populated region

688
33:38.570 --> 33:39.610
with plenty of people and grain.

689
33:39.610 --> 33:41.470
Supplies won't be a problem then.

690
33:42.750 --> 33:44.590
This campaign has another great significance.

691
33:44.590 --> 33:47.210
That is, the gate for us to move north to southern Gansu

692
33:47.210 --> 33:49.380
has been opened by our heroic Red Army.

693
33:49.750 --> 33:50.790
At this time,

694
33:50.920 --> 33:53.740
if the Left Route Army takes advantage of the KMT's thin forces

695
33:53.740 --> 33:55.030
and quickly advance north,

696
33:55.030 --> 33:56.140
joining forces with us will be

697
33:56.140 --> 33:57.470
just around the corner.

698
33:57.670 --> 33:58.690
The current problem is

699
33:58.690 --> 34:01.350
that the Left Route Army is on the south bank of the Gaqu River

700
34:01.350 --> 34:03.810
and doesn't seem to be making much progress.

701
34:07.460 --> 34:08.699
I have an idea.

702
34:09.219 --> 34:11.850
Can we have the Fourth Red Army send a regiment,

703
34:12.330 --> 34:13.520
taking some

704
34:13.650 --> 34:17.000
of the captured horses, yaks, and grain,

705
34:17.080 --> 34:18.610
to go south and back them up?

706
34:18.850 --> 34:21.050
Good, that's a good idea.

707
34:21.440 --> 34:23.659
We urge them in the telegrams and send troops to meet them.

708
34:23.659 --> 34:24.920
A two-pronged approach.

709
34:24.920 --> 34:26.080
The goal is

710
34:26.100 --> 34:28.380
to get the Left Route Army to move north quickly.

711
34:28.380 --> 34:28.810
Right.

712
34:28.830 --> 34:29.460
Now…

713
34:30.730 --> 34:34.250
Now, supplies are tight for us too.

714
34:35.820 --> 34:36.489
Yes.

715
34:37.110 --> 34:40.400
We're indeed having a hard time with supplies at present.

716
34:40.780 --> 34:44.139
But in order to get the Left Route Army to quickly move north,

717
34:44.429 --> 34:45.510
even if we have to tighten our belts,

718
34:45.510 --> 34:48.480
we must give these supplies to them.

719
34:48.590 --> 34:49.280
Right.

720
34:49.360 --> 34:51.880
Chiang Kai-shek only gave us these few days.

721
34:51.900 --> 34:54.010
We can't delay or wait.

722
34:54.510 --> 34:55.320
In addition,

723
34:55.340 --> 34:57.260
considering the supply difficulties in this area,

724
34:57.260 --> 35:00.580
the First Red Army can move north first

725
35:00.850 --> 35:02.040
from Baxi and Axirong

726
35:02.040 --> 35:04.040
to E'jie and rest and regroup there.

727
35:04.070 --> 35:06.870
Strategically, we can also seize the initiative.

728
35:08.030 --> 35:10.030
Comrades, the potatoes are cooked.

729
35:12.400 --> 35:14.650
Why do I smell yak meat?

730
35:15.290 --> 35:15.640
Is there?

731
35:15.640 --> 35:16.510
Everyone, take a sniff.

732
35:16.510 --> 35:16.940
Is there?

733
35:16.940 --> 35:17.900
Take a sniff.

734
35:18.000 --> 35:19.040
Yes, definitely.

735
35:19.440 --> 35:20.170
Smells good!

736
35:20.290 --> 35:22.000
Indeed, there is.

737
35:22.020 --> 35:24.460
Comrades, we're having yak meat!

738
35:25.120 --> 35:25.920
Inside, it is…

739
35:26.320 --> 35:27.360
Come eat yak meat!

740
35:27.360 --> 35:28.560
The smell of yak dung.

741
35:34.390 --> 35:37.710
[Chali Temple, Sichuan; Temporary Command Post of the Left Route Army]

742
35:36.240 --> 35:36.990
Great!

743
35:38.230 --> 35:40.650
Xiangqian fought this battle beautifully.

744
35:40.650 --> 35:41.330
Yes.

745
35:42.030 --> 35:44.630
The combat effectiveness of our 4th Front Army

746
35:45.240 --> 35:46.770
cannot be underestimated.

747
35:48.780 --> 35:50.300
Let me do it.

748
36:00.870 --> 36:01.640
Commander-in-Chief Zhu.

749
36:01.640 --> 36:02.640
Comrade Bocheng.

750
36:02.900 --> 36:04.360
You came at the right time.

751
36:04.540 --> 36:05.190
Hurry.

752
36:05.280 --> 36:07.950
[Huang Chao, Secretary-General of the Northwest Revolutionary Military Commission and the Sichuan-Shaanxi Provincial Soviet Government]

753
36:06.190 --> 36:07.900
Baozuo has been taken.

754
36:08.510 --> 36:10.590
This is a generous gift

755
36:10.610 --> 36:12.570
from Xiangqian and Changhao.

756
36:14.030 --> 36:14.880
This telegram

757
36:15.190 --> 36:17.630
not only brings us good news,

758
36:17.800 --> 36:20.050
but also urges us to head north as soon as possible

759
36:20.050 --> 36:21.130
to join them.

760
36:21.200 --> 36:21.640
Here.

761
36:23.150 --> 36:23.920
I know.

762
36:25.660 --> 36:27.570
I also want to head north as soon as possible.

763
36:26.670 --> 36:27.740
[Zhang Guotao, Member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Politburo]

764
36:27.740 --> 36:28.810
[Deputy Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission; General Political Commissar of the Red Army]

765
36:27.990 --> 36:29.050
But the problem is,

766
36:29.230 --> 36:30.460
with such heavy rain,

767
36:31.220 --> 36:33.420
it won't be easy to cross the Gaqu River.

768
36:33.860 --> 36:35.690
That's exactly why I came to see you.

769
36:35.690 --> 36:36.990
Dong Zhentang reported

770
36:36.990 --> 36:37.920
that this morning,

771
36:37.920 --> 36:39.980
he took people to the Gaqu River to test the crossing,

772
36:39.980 --> 36:42.050
proving that the troops can cross the river.

773
36:42.050 --> 36:42.820
But you

774
36:42.940 --> 36:44.330
not only sent people to stop him,

775
36:44.330 --> 36:45.510
but also disarmed him

776
36:45.510 --> 36:48.000
and threatened to investigate his past.

777
36:49.270 --> 36:51.180
Someone said he had problems in his past.

778
36:51.180 --> 36:52.090
What could I do?

779
36:52.650 --> 36:54.110
I couldn't just ignore it.

780
36:54.590 --> 36:57.720
Although Comrade Dong Zhentang is an uprising general,

781
36:57.760 --> 36:59.320
he, just like all commanders and fighters

782
36:59.320 --> 37:00.720
of the 5th Red Army Corps,

783
37:00.920 --> 37:02.480
has been serving as the rearguard

784
37:02.480 --> 37:04.510
since the beginning of the Long March.

785
37:04.510 --> 37:05.420
He's loyal to the CPC Central Committee

786
37:05.420 --> 37:07.170
and the Red Army.

787
37:07.370 --> 37:09.210
What past problems could he have?

788
37:09.210 --> 37:10.290
Comrade Guotao.

789
37:10.630 --> 37:13.830
The pressing task now is to cross the river and move north.

790
37:13.960 --> 37:15.030
We can't wait!

791
37:21.280 --> 37:22.550
Commander-in-Chief Zhu.

792
37:22.550 --> 37:25.380
I'd like you to seriously consider.

793
37:26.110 --> 37:29.160
Is crossing the river the only difficulty in moving north?

794
37:29.160 --> 37:30.880
With tens of thousands of troops on the move,

795
37:30.880 --> 37:33.620
even grain supply alone can't be guaranteed.

796
37:38.360 --> 37:40.160
There are indeed difficulties,

797
37:40.180 --> 37:42.970
but are they worse than what the Right Route Army faced?

798
37:42.970 --> 37:44.600
They still crossed the grassland

799
37:44.600 --> 37:45.800
and took Baozuo.

800
37:45.970 --> 37:47.230
Yes, Baozuo was taken.

801
37:47.290 --> 37:49.040
But they wiped out

802
37:49.060 --> 37:50.800
only three of Hu Zongnan's regiments.

803
37:50.800 --> 37:52.650
He still has more than 20 regiments.

804
37:52.650 --> 37:54.370
Even if we reach the southern Gansu area,

805
37:54.370 --> 37:57.400
Chiang Kai-shek still has nearly 80 regiments.

806
37:58.840 --> 38:01.390
There's also Ma Bufang's cavalry in Xiahe.

807
38:01.770 --> 38:04.300
Do you think there's a future in moving north?

808
38:09.110 --> 38:10.770
Fearing the enemy and not advancing.

809
38:10.770 --> 38:11.930
This is not the Red Army.

810
38:11.930 --> 38:15.060
Moths darting into a flame. It isn't the Red Army either.

811
38:15.110 --> 38:16.340
Then what do you want to do?

812
38:16.340 --> 38:17.070
It's simple.

813
38:17.330 --> 38:19.400
The Left Route Army returns to Aba first.

814
38:19.400 --> 38:21.820
We either establish the Chuankang base area in Aba

815
38:21.820 --> 38:23.220
or head south to Chengdu.

816
38:24.640 --> 38:25.370
Just as well,

817
38:25.590 --> 38:28.070
most of the 4th Front Army are from Sichuan,

818
38:28.210 --> 38:30.210
including you two,

819
38:30.390 --> 38:31.470
Commander-in-Chief

820
38:31.470 --> 38:32.680
and Comrade Bocheng.

821
38:33.100 --> 38:36.050
You'll have a bright future making revolution in your hometown.

822
38:36.050 --> 38:37.110
If this continues,

823
38:37.220 --> 38:38.870
the Red Army will split.

824
38:39.340 --> 38:42.000
If tens of thousands of Red Army troops split up,

825
38:42.110 --> 38:43.700
the consequences will be disastrous.

826
38:43.700 --> 38:45.710
We are not the ones who will suffer the disastrous consequences.

827
38:45.710 --> 38:47.530
The combat effectiveness of our 4th Front Army

828
38:47.530 --> 38:48.740
is still guaranteed.

829
38:49.920 --> 38:51.920
I've already drafted the telegram.

830
38:52.190 --> 38:55.360
If the Right Route Army doesn't want the Red Army to split up,

831
38:55.360 --> 38:58.720
then it should return to Songpan with the Left Route Army.

832
39:04.280 --> 39:06.140
So you had been planning all along

833
39:06.290 --> 39:07.760
to part ways with the Right Route Army.

834
39:07.760 --> 39:09.560
This is not called parting ways.

835
39:09.760 --> 39:11.630
This is taking the big picture into account.

836
39:11.630 --> 39:12.440
Sign it.

837
39:12.760 --> 39:15.490
If there's a problem, I'll take responsibility.

838
39:16.910 --> 39:18.940
I can't sign this.

839
39:21.150 --> 39:23.550
I only listen to the CPC Central Committee.

840
39:30.530 --> 39:31.990
He's not signing it again.

841
39:34.440 --> 39:37.440
Chairman, what about the signature on this telegram?

842
39:38.920 --> 39:40.030
The signature?

843
39:40.370 --> 39:41.900
Of course it cannot change.

844
39:42.360 --> 39:43.690
It's still Zhu De and me.

845
39:44.510 --> 39:45.880
We can't move north.

846
39:46.220 --> 39:47.660
This is fate.

847
39:48.180 --> 39:49.010
So,

848
39:50.280 --> 39:53.890
blame the Gaqu River.

849
39:56.630 --> 39:57.690
You can't blame me.

850
39:57.780 --> 39:58.570
Send it as is.

851
39:59.320 --> 39:59.990
Yes, sir.

852
40:19.520 --> 40:20.560
Outrageous!

853
40:20.910 --> 40:21.870
Outrageous!

854
40:22.150 --> 40:23.110
So many excuses.

855
40:23.230 --> 40:24.750
None of them hold water.

856
40:27.190 --> 40:29.520
They can't even cross the mere Gaqu River?

857
40:30.190 --> 40:31.730
Didn't we cross the Wujiang River

858
40:31.730 --> 40:33.330
and Jinsha River just fine?

859
40:35.480 --> 40:37.810
They can't even cross the mere Gaqu River?

860
40:40.810 --> 40:43.790
Didn't the 4th Front Army cross the Jialing River too?

861
40:43.790 --> 40:45.410
Not only do they refuse to move north

862
40:45.410 --> 40:46.410
and return to Aba,

863
40:46.820 --> 40:50.220
they also want our Right Route Army to go back down to Songpan.

864
40:52.430 --> 40:53.560
Comrade Xiangqian,

865
40:53.890 --> 40:54.950
Comrade Changhao,

866
40:55.300 --> 40:56.470
what are your opinions?

867
40:56.470 --> 40:57.670
I have no objections.

868
40:58.320 --> 40:59.030
I think

869
40:59.140 --> 41:02.060
the Central Committee's policy of continuing to move north is correct.

870
41:02.060 --> 41:03.870
I also agree with the Central Committee's policy.

871
41:03.870 --> 41:06.460
The two front armies should stay united.

872
41:09.620 --> 41:10.340
Great.

873
41:11.150 --> 41:12.030
Comrade Changhao.

874
41:12.030 --> 41:13.160
Comrade Xiangqian.

875
41:13.570 --> 41:16.170
It's a good thing that you two can agree with the Central Committee.

876
41:16.170 --> 41:18.000
It's a very good thing.

877
41:18.250 --> 41:19.610
When it comes to Comrade Guotao,

878
41:19.610 --> 41:20.780
ten words from us

879
41:21.330 --> 41:23.590
are not as effective as one word from you two.

880
41:23.590 --> 41:24.680
I suggest

881
41:24.970 --> 41:27.210
you send another telegram to Comrade Guotao

882
41:27.210 --> 41:29.170
in your own names

883
41:29.490 --> 41:31.360
and advise him to move north immediately.

884
41:31.360 --> 41:33.730
Okay, we'll go back and send it right away.

885
41:41.990 --> 41:43.690
The first signature on this telegram

886
41:43.690 --> 41:44.930
is Zhu De.

887
41:44.960 --> 41:47.150
Comrade Zhu De would never do something

888
41:47.150 --> 41:48.710
contrary to the Central Committee's policy.

889
41:48.710 --> 41:49.940
The sending of this telegram

890
41:49.940 --> 41:52.960
can only be the result of Zhang Guotao acting arbitrarily.

891
41:52.960 --> 41:53.960
At this point,

892
41:54.150 --> 41:55.360
we must be prepared.

893
41:55.420 --> 41:57.550
If Zhang Guotao refuses to move north,

894
41:57.670 --> 41:58.920
I'm afraid

895
41:58.940 --> 42:00.960
not only will the plan to move north to southern Gansu be thwarted,

896
42:00.960 --> 42:03.070
but we may also face

897
42:03.150 --> 42:04.590
other risks.

898
42:06.110 --> 42:09.150
On the principled question of moving north or moving south,

899
42:09.150 --> 42:11.880
no matter what dangers we may encounter,

900
42:12.110 --> 42:14.680
we must never make any compromises.

901
42:23.400 --> 42:24.150
Comrades,

902
42:24.760 --> 42:27.280
just like crossing the Xiang River,

903
42:27.510 --> 42:29.710
we've reached another critical moment

904
42:29.770 --> 42:32.030
that will decide our future and destiny.

905
42:39.530 --> 42:43.550
[Panzhou Village, Sichuan; Frontline General Headquarters]

906
42:43.020 --> 42:45.620
Comrades, please step out for a moment.

907
42:45.900 --> 42:46.570
Okay.

908
42:46.980 --> 42:47.910
You too.

909
42:49.340 --> 42:50.010
Okay.

910
42:53.250 --> 42:55.240
How should we reply to this telegram?

911
42:55.240 --> 42:56.360
What do you think?

912
42:57.480 --> 43:00.050
I agree with the Central Committee's policy to move north.

913
43:00.050 --> 43:02.550
But Chairman Zhang's intention is very clear.

914
43:02.550 --> 43:03.600
He refuses to move north.
